# only wrote the framed keep-alive every 200 ms: no start, SetSpeed, pause or stop in it.
# Speed scale (SPEC 3.7): every status frame has @3 = @5 = 0b 54 = 2900. Over the file the belt's
# distance (u32 @7, metres) goes 633 -> 902 m between its first and last change, while its session
# time (u32 @20, ms) goes 770000 -> 1104000: 269 m in 334.0 s = 2.899 km/h. As km/h x 1000 the
# status reads 2.900; as mph x 1600 it would read 2.917, outside the 1 m / 1 frame margin.
